# =============================================================================
# .gitattributes
#
# RULE
#   Every text file is LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on every
#   platform. Nothing here changes what a file says. It fixes only how a line
#   ends, so that the same file has the same checksum wherever it is checked
#   out.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#   Without it, git on Windows stores LF and writes CRLF into the working tree.
#   A Linux clone then holds LF. The two are the same table and they have
#   different checksums, and on 2026-08-03 that stopped a run at stage 0: the
#   master tables in the repository and the copies in the published archive were
#   byte for byte identical on Windows and differed by 481 carriage returns on
#   the cluster.
#
#   The same difference moves config_hash, which every result row carries. The
#   same config.yaml has to hash to the same value on the machine that writes
#   the paper and on the machine that runs the pipeline, or the provenance
#   stamp records the platform rather than the configuration.
# =============================================================================

# Text is LF everywhere. git detects which files are text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Audio and archives are never line-ending converted. These are named because a
# corrupted wav is silent damage, and detection is not worth relying on here.
*.wav binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.aup3 binary
